### ==========================================
### ORDER SERVICE - REST API
### ==========================================
### Register a customer first (Customer Service, port 8080) and use its
### customerCode below - Order Service will reject an unknown customer.

### 1. Place an order (subtotal < RM100 -> RM5 delivery fee applies)
POST http://localhost:8082/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerCode": "CUSXXXXXXXXXXXX",
  "restaurantCode": "REST001",
  "deliveryAddress": "12A, Jalan Example, 40150 Shah Alam, Selangor",
  "items": [
    { "menuItemCode": "MENU-NASI-LEMAK", "itemName": "Nasi Lemak Ayam", "quantity": 2, "unitPrice": 12.50 },
    { "menuItemCode": "MENU-TEH-O", "itemName": "Teh O Ais", "quantity": 2, "unitPrice": 3.00 }
  ]
}


### 2. Place an order that qualifies for free delivery (subtotal >= RM100)
POST http://localhost:8082/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerCode": "CUSXXXXXXXXXXXX",
  "restaurantCode": "REST001",
  "deliveryAddress": "12A, Jalan Example, 40150 Shah Alam, Selangor",
  "items": [
    { "menuItemCode": "MENU-SET-A", "itemName": "Family Feast Set", "quantity": 4, "unitPrice": 30.00 }
  ]
}


### 3. Get all orders
GET http://localhost:8082/orders


### 4. Get order by order code
### Replace ORDXXXXXXXXXXXXX with the code returned from placing an order
GET http://localhost:8082/orders/ORDXXXXXXXXXXXXX


### 5. Get all orders for a customer
GET http://localhost:8082/orders/customer/CUSXXXXXXXXXXXX


### 6. Cancel an order (only works while status is still PLACED)
### Replace ORDXXXXXXXXXXXXX with the code returned from placing an order
PUT http://localhost:8082/orders/ORDXXXXXXXXXXXXX/cancel


### 7. Placing an order for a customer that does not exist -> 400 Bad Request
POST http://localhost:8082/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerCode": "CUS_DOES_NOT_EXIST",
  "restaurantCode": "REST001",
  "deliveryAddress": "Nowhere",
  "items": [
    { "menuItemCode": "MENU-NASI-LEMAK", "itemName": "Nasi Lemak Ayam", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 12.50 }
  ]
}


### ==========================================
### KAFKA DEMONSTRATION
### ==========================================
### Order Service publishes "order.placed" whenever step 1/2/8 above
### succeeds - watch the console log or http://localhost:8085 (Kafka UI,
### if the customer-service docker-compose port is used) to see it land.
###
### To see the consumer side working before the Restaurant & Catalog and
### Delivery services exist, publish a fake event manually from a Kafka
### console producer (adjust to your Kafka image's CLI path):
###
###   docker exec -it nomnom-kafka /opt/kafka/bin/kafka-console-producer.sh \
###     --topic order.confirmed --broker-list localhost:9092
###
### then paste (single line):
###   {"orderId":"ORDXXXXXXXXXXXXX","restaurantCode":"REST001","status":"CONFIRMED"}
###
### GET the order afterwards - status should now show CONFIRMED.
